   m_sSRZReadText "Electrical fields. Field E-3. The discharge comes before you see it. Hair stands up, the dosimeter crackles, the air smells of a storm. Anything metal inside two metres draws the arc. Rubber soles help a little. A thrown bolt sets the field off and it needs about four seconds to charge again. Count to five, then walk. Two lab assistants did not count."
